  "abstract": "Memory is essential for long-horizon robotic manipulation, where agents must retain task-relevant information over extended interactions. Existing approaches either expand the policy's historical context or compress history at the risk of discarding useful information. We introduce Mem4Act, which consolidates historical experience into a fixed-size latent memory interface to the action policy. Mem4Act addresses coverage of long histories through multi-granularity temporal aggregation, content preservation through semantic QA and keyframe DINO reconstruction, and utilization for control through memory-first two-stage training. On long-horizon, memory-intensive manipulation, it achieves 49.88% success on RoboMME, 61.0% on RMBench, and 81.50% on real-world tasks.",
