  "abstract": "Instructions such as \"pick up the object moved last\" require event history, even when the target is now occluded. BeyondSCe connects video reasoning to active view selection without task-specific training. An off-the-shelf model identifies the target, while its historical 3D observations provide an event prior for spatial search. A target belief is revised by new evidence and guides camera motion, discounting visibility through unknown space. Across 150 real-robot trials, grasp success reaches 76.7%, versus 50.0% for the strongest baseline. On 20 additional heavily occluded trials, the event prior reduces mean views from 4.00 to 2.20 at the same observed 95% grasp success.",
