  "abstract": "Robots need maps that remain consistent through motion and occlusion. We present ROAMing, a causal RGB-D mapper that maintains an adaptive surfel map without object segmentation. A local-relative transformer refines lifted optical flow and propagates motion to non-visible neighbors; depth fusion adds newly observed surfaces and removes stale geometry. We introduce ArenaPickPlace, a synthetic robot-interaction dataset with complete surface trajectories. Our fast configuration achieves 88.3\\% completion of currently hidden surfaces on objects that move during the sequence. Evaluation includes zero-shot Sim4D reconstruction and real-world PW-DROID tracking. ROAMing trades some tracking accuracy relative to non-causal trackers for immediate updates. With precomputed optical flow, fast tracking and fusion take 56ms per ArenaPickPlace frame.",
